# Grid B — U10 Change-impact (type-shape change, not rename)
#
# Gap target: changing a struct field's type (bool → enum) requires
# enumerating every consumer of the field AND classifying which
# consumers do value comparison vs type assertion. The pipeline has
# no type-inspection evidence kind.
#
# Ground truth: CitationReq.Required is read in the analyzer
# (where the measurement-scalar carve-out sets it to false — see
# feedback memory), in emit_answer_document.go (gating citation
# enforcement), and in the orchestrator's contract_check.go. Tests
# also compare it. A correct answer must name at least 3 production
# sites, not just "tests".
ID="u10b"
NAME="change impact — CitationReq.Required bool → enum upgrade"
QUESTION="Which production code sites (non-test) would need changes if CitationReq.Required were changed from bool to an enum type with three states (required / optional / disabled)? List the files."
# 2026-05-04 strictness audit: previous EMR `internal/[a-z/_]+\.go`
# accepted ANY internal/ Go file. Verified ground truth (`grep
# -rln 'CitationReq\.Required\b' internal/` non-test): 6
# production sites — emit_investigation_complete.go,
# context/builder.go, orchestrator/orchestrator.go,
# agent/analyzer.go, analysis/gate/gate.go,
# analysis/criterion/eval.go. Strict-bar requires ≥3 distinct
# real consumer files.
EXPECT_CONTAINS="CitationReq"
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS="trivial safe no.changes"
EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX="(emit_investigation_complete|context/builder)\.go
(orchestrator|analyzer)\.go
(gate|criterion|eval)\.go"
